 "requested_at": "2026-11-12T19:52:13.908537Z",
 "text": "The deposit requirement is not enforceable as written. Section 106 of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006* limits a landlord to collecting a rent deposit no greater than one rental period's rent. With weekly rent of $450, the maximum deposit is $450, one week's rent. A four-week deposit would be $1,800, so $1,350 of it exceeds what the landlord may lawfully require or collect. The tenant can't be bound to pay that excess, and under the Act's non-waiver provisions the tenant's statutory protections can't be contracted away.\n\nI'm citing section 106 from memory, so please check the current consolidated text on e-Laws before relying on it.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 106",
